<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-ENDOKRININIAI POSTS LOWER NET PROFIT IN H1 97.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-ENDOKRININIAI POSTS LOWER NET PROFIT IN H1 97.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first half of 1997,</p>
<p>					(million litas unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     712,000     vs 865,000</p>
<p>    Turnover			 11.12	 vs 8.8</p>
<p>    Operating costs		6.94	  vs 5.3</p>
<p>    Gross profit		   4.18	  vs 3.47</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     1.14	  vs 874,000</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		 1.05	  vs 914,000</p>
<p>NOTE -- Endokrinininai Preparatai , a</p>
<p>pharmaceutical producer, is an A Group company listed on</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse.</p>
<p>- The company posted a net profit of 2.2 million litas on</p>
<p>turnover of 19.3 million litas in 1996.</p>
<p>- The company's finance official Gediminas Jagelevichius</p>
<p>told Reuters that the firm's net profit was down because the</p>
<p>company had to pay a regular 29 percent profit tax when the</p>
<p>five percent profit tax was abolished.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
